# SPA routing for the app's own routes — deliberately NOT a `/*` catch-all.
#
# Express serves index.html for any non-/api path in dev and under `npm start`
# (server/src/app.ts:24-26), but a static host has no such rule, so a direct hit
# on /privacy, /terms or /contact would 404 instead of booting the app.
#
# Cloudflare's docs say "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or
# not an asset matches the incoming request". Read literally, a `/*` rule would
# rewrite /assets/*.js to HTML too, and the app would die on a MIME-type error
# rather than a 404. Naming the routes instead — these are the ones in
# client/src/App.tsx — behaves identically whether or not that reading is right.
# Anything else gets a real 404, which is the honest answer for a static site.
/app        /index.html  200
/privacy    /index.html  200
/terms      /index.html  200
/contact    /index.html  200
